DTSTAMP:20260513T025252Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51763879205860
DTSTART:20260419T011500Z
DTEND:20260419T021500Z
DESCRIPTION:Ticket show holders for UP's theater production of The Lightnin
 g Thief may enjoy a complimentary small bites reception and an expert pre-
 show panel discussion. Ticket purchase HERE. Saturday\, April 18\, Mago Hu
 nt Center. Reception at 6:15pm\; Panel Discussion from 6:45-7:15pm\; Show 
 at 7:30pm. For more information and ADA accommodations contact garaventa@u
 p.edu and 503-943-7702.\n\nAbout The Lightning Thief: “As the half-blood
  son of a Greek god\, Percy Jackson has newly-discovered powers he can't c
 ontrol\, a destiny he doesn't want\, and a mythology textbook's worth of m
 onsters on his trail. When Zeus's master lightning bolt is stolen and Perc
 y becomes the prime suspect\, he has to find and return the bolt to prove 
 his innocence and prevent a war between the gods…Adapted from the best-s
 elling book The Lightning Thief by Rick Riordan and featuring a thrilling 
 original rock score\, The Lightning Thief: The Percy Jackson Musical is an
  action-packed mythical adventure "worthy of the gods" (Time Out New York)
 .
GEO:45.573252;-122.728181
LOCATION:Mago Hunt Center\, Lobby and Theater
SUMMARY:Theater Pre-Play Reception & Panel: "The Lightning Thief: The Percy
  Jackson Musical"
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.up.edu/event/copy-of-theater-pre-play-recept
 ion-panel-the-revolutionists
CATEGORIES:Performance
CATEGORIES:Social Gathering / Reception
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260513T025252Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52339988338409
DTSTART:20260419T023000Z
DTEND:20260419T033000Z
DESCRIPTION:⚡️Ancient myth and teen angst collide in this high-voltage 
 rock musical adapted from Rick Riordan’s best-selling novel\, where youn
 g people learn that the things that make us different are the things that 
 make us strong. \n \nDemigod Percy Jackson has always struggled with fitti
 ng in. When his single mom must send him where she can’t follow\, he end
 s up at a summer camp for kids like him – half Greek god\, half mortal. 
 Joined by a daughter of Athena trying to prove her worth and a satyr tryin
 g to make up for past tragedies\, the trio journeys into the underworld an
 d back to reclaim Zeus’s stolen lightning bolt and stop a war between th
 e gods. With a whole host of mythological creatures chasing after them\, c
 an these unlikely heroes shoulder the fate of the world? Maybe Percy can f
 inally find a place where he belongs...if he doesn’t die first. This ele
 ctric coming-of-age story will resonate with anyone who’s had trouble fi
 nding the courage to stand strong in a world full of monsters.\n\nTickets 
 are on sale now for this incredible show\, running April 8-12 and 15-19. T
 he Lightning Thief will be the raucous conclusion to an amazing UPTheater 
 season! Get your tickets now before they’re gone! 💙 Use code 'FIRST50
 ' for $5 tickets\, and 'PRESALE' for $10 tickets!
GEO:45.573252;-122.728181
LOCATION:Mago Hunt Center
SUMMARY:The Lightning Thief: The Percy Jackson Musical
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.up.edu/event/the-lightning-thief-the-percy-j
 ackson-musical
CATEGORIES:Performance
END:VEVENT
